/E ( For the Christian, this hope is deeper still: our worth is not determined by age, productivity, income, physical strength, or social position, but by the love and calling of God. Let us therefore honor our senior citizens, care for them with dignity, invite them into meaningful participation, and receive from them the spiritual heritage they have accumulated through a lifetime of walking with God.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 642 0 R
/E (September also gives us an opportunity to reflect on our responsibilities as citizens. Constitution Day and Citizenship Day on September 17 remind us of the importance of constitutional principles, civic responsibility, justice, freedom, and the privileges and responsibilities of citizenship. As Christians living in the United States, we are called to be faithful followers of Christ and responsible citizens, respecting the dignity of every person, upholding truth, pursuing justice, and contributing positively to society. Our Christian identity should never lead us away from responsible citizenship; rather, it should inspire us to become people of integrity, compassion, honesty, and peace wherever God has placed us.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
